  "contentHtml": "<p>1. <a href=\"https://pod.link/6827686888\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">New Texas A&amp;M podcast: Economists Unscripted</a>.</p>\n<p>2. <a href=\"https://x.com/paulnovosad/status/2120155142674620590\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A new tool for AI-proof homework assignments</a>.&nbsp; “<span>It’s called </span><a href=\"https://t.co/hLyeoN98Lp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">deb8.tv</a><span> — students get paired and have live video debates with one another.”</span></p>\n<p>3. “<a href=\"https://x.com/JesusFerna7026/status/2120197249485676780\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The average French person believes there are 6.4 workers for every retiree. The real number is about 1.8.</a>”</p>\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/10/science/sulfuric-acid-elixir-of-life.html?unlocked_article_code=1.PVE.7DsC.OCS-DMl1-o8w&amp;smid=url-share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sulfuric acid as a basic medium for life?</a> (NYT)</p>\n<p>5. <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/2026/12/aquaterra-ancient-human-migration/689029/?gift=KYf_V7WJ7ea9idDTnMyY9PYpLlJPtgC44FLySHU726g&amp;utm_source=copy-link&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_campaign=share\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The fascination of underwater archaeology</a> (Atlantic).</p>\n<p>6. <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/us/richard-posner-dead.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NYT obituary for Richard Posner</a>.&nbsp; And <a href=\"https://casssunstein.substack.com/p/on-richard-posner?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=3391848&amp;post_id=224593419&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cass Sunstein on Richard Posner</a>.</p>",
